      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The test checks that `Hex.encodeHex` produces lowercase by default and uppercase when `toLowerCase=false`. The original class carries many unused helper methods and imports that obscure the single focused test. I'll clean those up and add clarifying variable names and comments.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused helper methods and imports, renames `b` to `helloWorldBytes` and `expected` to `expectedUpperCaseHex` for clarity, and adds inline comments explaining the intent of each assertion."
